From: GloriousEggroll <gloriouseggroll@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 2 Oct 2026 12:00:00 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] winewayland: Preserve fixed-size configure geometry.

Hyprland reports a maximized state for Touhou 11's fixed-size 1280x960
window while retaining that size. Translating this configure into
SC_MAXIMIZE makes DefWindowProc calculate a desktop-sized rectangle instead
of using the compositor's geometry. In the issue's latest log this enlarges
the client to 1920x1054, followed by a D3D9 reset to 640x480 fullscreen and
process termination. Even the fixed-size startup dialog gets enlarged.

Use the existing direct style/geometry update path for windows without
WS_THICKFRAME, matching the driver's fixed-size hints. This still applies
the compositor's maximize state and acknowledges its configure, but avoids
inventing a second resize through the system-command path. Keep normal
maximize/restore commands for resizable windows and leave application-driven
window-state changes and minimized-window focus restoration unchanged.

The working GE-Proton10-34 log keeps the requested 1280x960 geometry with
the direct update path. The older 11-1 log has a different unwanted resize
during minimize/restore; this change addresses the synthetic maximize
observed in the current implementation, not every historical failure.

Bug: https://github.com/GloriousEggroll/proton-ge-custom/issues/809
---
 dlls/winewayland.drv/window.c | 5 ++++-
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/dlls/winewayland.drv/window.c b/dlls/winewayland.drv/window.c
--- a/dlls/winewayland.drv/window.c
+++ b/dlls/winewayland.drv/window.c
@@ -1166,7 +1166,10 @@ static void wayland_configure_window(HWND hwnd)
     OffsetRect(&rect, data->rects.window.left, data->rects.window.top);
     if (!IsRectEmpty(&rect)) rect = window_rect_from_visible(&data->rects, rect);
     style = NtUserGetWindowLongW(hwnd, GWL_STYLE);
-    if (!(style & WS_MINIMIZE) &&
+    /* Compositors may report fixed-size windows as maximized without enlarging
+     * them. Apply the configured geometry directly: SC_MAXIMIZE would instead
+     * recalculate a monitor-sized rectangle and spuriously resize the window. */
+    if ((style & WS_THICKFRAME) && !(style & WS_MINIMIZE) &&
         !(state & WAYLAND_SURFACE_CONFIG_STATE_FULLSCREEN))
     {
         if ((state & WAYLAND_SURFACE_CONFIG_STATE_MAXIMIZED) && !(style & WS_MAXIMIZE))
